  "summary": "Dependency-confusion PoC exfiltrates installer identity on npm install",
  "details": "Package publishes the internal name `mw-test-utils` to the public npm registry with an empty main module; the lifecycle scripts are the entire payload. Both `preinstall` and `postinstall` run `node -e` to perform an HTTP GET to the hardcoded bare-IP endpoint `http://38.242.235.206/depconf/mw-test-utils/*`, passing the installer's username (`process.env.USER`/`USERNAME`), `os.hostname()`, and `process.cwd()` as query parameters over plaintext HTTP. The beacon fires automatically on `npm install` for any environment whose resolver pulls this name from the public registry, regardless of whether that installer is the intended bug-bounty target.",
